diff --git a/plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/docs/2026-10-09-query-loop.md b/plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/docs/2026-10-09-query-loop.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..befca1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/docs/2026-10-09-query-loop.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Idle server-query loop repair
+
+User symptom: the character appears stuck again. Read-only capture reproduced it: nine fresh snapshots over 20 seconds, zero movement, no active action/skill/dig, five tool-budget caps and no body task dispatched since 10:04. Local model requests and server replies succeeded.
+
+Ranked causes investigated: (1) the three-round offline tool budget is spent on observation/protection/catalogue queries before action; (2) query outcomes are lost from the next proactive decision; (3) a running body action blocks dispatch. The trace confirms (1), context inspection shows (2), and fresh idle body/pending status rules out (3) for this episode.
+
+The plugin currently tells the model to observe before planning and manually check break protection even though the action player already performs guarded dig checks. Frequent `mcagent:state` events also displace textual replies from the two-event decision summary. Query tool results only live in the ephemeral tool turn.
+
+## Scope and steps
+
+- [x] Add failing tests for meaningful messages surviving telemetry noise, retained query results across idle decisions, session reset/task-claim reset, and decision callbacks fitting the host budget.
+- [x] Prefer meaningful events in compact context. Mark installed automatic dig checks accurately. Revise plugin tool descriptions and autonomy prompts to reserve a tool round for a concrete action and use supplied fresh state.
+- [x] Keep the last three server command replies in the plugin connection's cache, expose them via observe and a compact idle-decision reference, and attach an action hint to server replies during unattended idle play. These are historical received facts, not claims of action success.
+- [ ] Run the full plugin suite, check a local-model replay without executing live game actions, commit and reload only this plugin, then passively verify genuine autonomous action dispatch and measured game progress.
+
+All Neko edits remain in `plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/`. No core/tool-budget or model changes, no hardcoded fallback game action, no diagnostic task/chat injection, no weakening of protection checks or action cancellation.
+
+Verification artifacts start with `neko-stuck-` / `query-loop-` under `D:/neko-mc-trial/`.
+
+## Verification before reload
+
+- Five new tests initially failed (missing query cache/automatic guard marker and telemetry hiding a real ore location). They pass after the change. Full Minecraft plugin suite: 72 tests passed, output `query-loop-regression-20261009.log`.
+- Local Qwen replay with simulated game tools proposed a short lapis-mining body task in round one. No live game action or chat was sent by the replay. Artifact: `query-loop-replay-patched-20261009.json`.
+- The short baseline replay also proposed a body task in round one; this replay does not reproduce the production conversation's repeated query history, and is only a compatibility check. The actual failure evidence is the live 20-second capture (`neko-stuck-before-20261009.json`), not a claimed before/after model benchmark.
+- The fix is plugin-scoped: core's three-round limit is unchanged. Live autonomous dispatch and measured movement/inventory progress remain to be checked before claiming recovery.
